{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>You shall not kindle fire.</b> The Torah warned about kindling more than other labors, because it is not as obviously a labor, and perhaps they will say: we are not doing a labor, but we will kindle the fire and prepare everything, in order to work with gold and silver immediately after the Sabbath — therefore it is stated: 'You shall not kindle.' And in tractate Shabbat our Rabbis disagreed: there is one who says kindling went out as a negative commandment, and there is one who says it went out to separate."], :book :exodus, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 35, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:04:44.261268218Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}